1
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:04,000
Oh, you're home.

2
00:00:04,533 --> 00:00:07,367
I got the stains out, okay?
It's not off-white anymore.

3
00:00:07,367 --> 00:00:09,767
White just comes out different
when it's hand-washed

4
00:00:09,767 --> 00:00:11,167
and sun-dried.

5
00:00:15,567 --> 00:00:18,433
- Why'd you even wash my rags...
- Hey!

6
00:00:18,433 --> 00:00:19,767
That's not a rag!

7
00:00:19,767 --> 00:00:23,767
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

8
00:00:23,767 --> 00:00:25,467
Don't tell me you still
wear this!

9
00:00:25,467 --> 00:00:26,633
Hey! Why not?

10
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,433
It still covers what it's
supposed to cover.

11
00:00:29,433 --> 00:00:33,033
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

12
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:34,100
Here.

13
00:00:39,133 --> 00:00:40,733
[PHONE CHIMES]

14
00:00:44,067 --> 00:00:47,667
"June, can I borrow some money?"

15
00:00:48,067 --> 00:00:49,300
[MUSIC STOPS]

16
00:00:54,667 --> 00:00:56,333
[PHONE RINGING]

17
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:00,167
Hey.

18
00:01:00,167 --> 00:01:02,700
- [RINGING CONTINUES]
- Your Uncle Dennis is calling.

19
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:04,233
He's asking to borrow money.

20
00:01:05,367 --> 00:01:07,700
He needs it to pay
for his dentures.

21
00:01:09,167 --> 00:01:10,633
What are you going to lend him?

22
00:01:10,633 --> 00:01:12,533
You don't have any money,
remember?

23
00:01:12,533 --> 00:01:14,067
You lost your job.

24
00:01:15,433 --> 00:01:17,767
- [RINGING CONTINUES]
- It's a sin to turn him down.

25
00:01:21,067 --> 00:01:22,067
[BEEPS]

26
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,400
Hello, Uncle Dennis!

27
00:01:26,333 --> 00:01:29,667
I'm a little short on cash
right now.

28
00:01:34,067 --> 00:01:35,400
Oh, okay.

29
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:37,700
Just send me your QR code
so I can transfer it.

30
00:01:39,067 --> 00:01:40,167
Bye.

31
00:01:41,333 --> 00:01:42,533
[BEEPS]

32
00:01:42,533 --> 00:01:44,500
I thought you were going
to say no.

33
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:46,533
I just feel bad for him.

34
00:01:46,533 --> 00:01:48,233
It's hard not having dentures.

35
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,733
But you are
the one who suffers.

36
00:01:50,333 --> 00:01:53,133
You know, if there's
one thing I learned

37
00:01:53,133 --> 00:01:55,167
from what happened to Donato,

38
00:01:55,167 --> 00:01:56,767
it's that money doesn't run out.

39
00:01:57,733 --> 00:02:02,200
But family can be gone
in an instant.

40
00:02:03,867 --> 00:02:05,033
Yeah.

41
00:02:05,033 --> 00:02:07,567
I help them not because
I'm obligated to.

42
00:02:08,633 --> 00:02:10,433
I do it because I want to.

43
00:02:10,733 --> 00:02:12,233
Family is family, right?

44
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:14,600
I've already got
so little family left.

45
00:02:14,633 --> 00:02:16,500
Why would I be stingy with them?

46
00:02:17,467 --> 00:02:21,400
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

47
00:02:22,533 --> 00:02:24,633
They're arguing again.

48
00:02:24,633 --> 00:02:31,500
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

49
00:02:53,233 --> 00:02:54,567
<i> Oh, sorry!</i>

50
00:02:54,567 --> 00:02:56,633
<i>I got thirsty.
You're just so hot!</i>

51
00:02:57,433 --> 00:02:58,900
<i> Papa Ping and I are okay now.</i>

52
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:01,333
<i>- Does he love you too?
- Ow!</i>

53
00:03:01,333 --> 00:03:03,533
<i>Isn't it better if you really
get to know each other</i>

54
00:03:03,533 --> 00:03:05,167
<i> before you get married?</i>

55
00:03:06,767 --> 00:03:10,167
<i>Based on the forensic findings,
someone sabotaged Donato.</i>

56
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:12,800
<i>The yacht didn't sink
by accident.</i>

57
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:14,000
<i> Be careful.</i>

58
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,433
<i>Most of the time, it's
someone close to the family.</i>
